---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { REMOVAL_ADDRESS } from "../lib/launch.ts";
---

<Base>
  <div class="wrap section-y">
    <div class="max-w-xl">
      <h1 class="page-title text-ink mb-4">Privacy</h1>
      <p class="text-sm text-ink-2 mb-6">Effective date: 25 September 2026.</p>
      <p class="text-sm text-ink-2 mb-6">
        The Rupee Fund is a FOSS United community initiative run by community members. The community
        team manages the launch notification list. We adopt the privacy standards in the <a
          href="https://fossunited.org/privacy-policy"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class="inline-link">FOSS United privacy policy</a
        >, dated 7 February 2024, with the local rules below. These local rules define our data use
        and take precedence where the source differs. We do not adopt the source’s wider uses for
        marketing, profiling, event tickets, or ownership transfers. Foundation roles named in the
        source do not become roles in The Rupee Fund through adoption. Later changes to the source
        do not change this policy automatically.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl text-ink mt-10 mb-3">What we collect</h2>
      <ul class="text-sm text-ink-2 mb-6 list-disc pl-5 space-y-1">
        <li>Your name.</li>
        <li>Your email address.</li>
        <li>The time of your consent, signup, and latest update.</li>
        <li>The page that you used to join.</li>
        <li>The amount each month that you say you can give.</li>
        <li>The number of months that you say you can give, if you answer.</li>
        <li>The question that you ask the team, if you ask one.</li>
        <li>Whether you tick the box for monthly updates.</li>
        <li>Which of FOSS user, FOSS contributor and student you tick, if you tick any.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="text-sm text-ink-2 mb-6">
        We keep this data to send you one email when the fund opens, to send you monthly updates if
        you tick the box, and to plan the fund. Your answers about money bind you to nothing. We
        take no payment. We hold no payment details. Access to your answers is limited to the people
        who administer the list and the services that process it.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl text-ink mt-10 mb-3">Storage and retention</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-ink-2 mb-6">
        Cloudflare hosts this site and stores the list. The team can export the list to prepare the
        launch email. We retain entries for launch planning and notification. We have not set a
        fixed deletion date. Removal from the mailing list retains your entry as described below.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl text-ink mt-10 mb-3">Your IP address</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-ink-2 mb-6">
        We read your IP address when you send the form. We use it to prevent abuse. When your
        browser runs JavaScript, we also send it to Cloudflare with the bot check below. We do not
        store it in your list entry. Cloudflare also processes connection data to provide hosting
        and abuse protection.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl text-ink mt-10 mb-3">Bot protection</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-ink-2 mb-6">
        When your browser runs JavaScript, the form uses Cloudflare Turnstile to tell a person apart
        from a bot. Cloudflare states what Turnstile collects in the <a
          href="https://www.cloudflare.com/turnstile-privacy-policy/"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class="inline-link">Turnstile Privacy Addendum</a
        >.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl text-ink mt-10 mb-3">Profile photos</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-ink-2 mb-6">
        The Team page loads profile photos from GitHub. GitHub receives your IP address when your
        browser requests these photos.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl text-ink mt-10 mb-3">How to leave the list</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-ink-2">
        Send an email to <a href={`mailto:${REMOVAL_ADDRESS}`} class="inline-link"
          >{REMOVAL_ADDRESS}</a
        >. We take you off the list. We keep your entry, and we mark it as removed, so that a later
        signup cannot add you again. Ask at any time.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
